%SIXMD 1
# @?LOGDRAIN - DRAIN THE PERSISTENT LOGSTORE

## @?OPERANDS

### @?[STRING]
STATUS, FOLLOW, NULL, FILE, CONSOLE, OR MTC MODE AND ITS BOUNDED ARGUMENTS.

## DESCRIPTION

LOGDRAIN IS THE PRIVILEGED PROCESS CONTEXT CONSUMER OF THE KERNEL LOGSTORE.
IT CAN REPORT STATUS, DISCARD VALIDATED RECORDS, APPEND RAW RECORDS TO THE
SYSTEM LOG FILE, PRINT RECORDS TO A CONSOLE, OR WRITE THEM TO MAGNETIC TAPE.

FOLLOW WAITS FOR NEW PRODUCER RECORDS AFTER CATCHING UP.  THE PERSISTENT DRAIN
CURSOR ADVANCES ONLY AFTER THE SELECTED SINK ACCEPTS A COMPLETE RECORD.

## @?FILES

### @?/LOG/SYSTEM.LOG
CURRENT FILE SINK.

### @?/LOG/SYSTEM.OLD
PREVIOUS ROTATED FILE SINK.

## @?EXIT STATUS

### @?0 - OPERATION COMPLETED
### @?1 - INVALID MODE, PRIVILEGE FAILURE, OR SINK ERROR
